<title>USA: Consolidated Eco-Systems gets contracts.</title>
<headline>Consolidated Eco-Systems gets contracts.</headline>
<dateline>LITTLE ROCK, Ark. 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated Eco-Systems Inc, formerly Exsorbet Industries Inc, said its Industrial Services Division has entered into two agreements with clients which are anticipated to produce $2 million in gross revenues over the next 12 months.</p>
<p>The agreements call for Consolidated Eco to perform work on a time-and-materials basis at two facilities in Alabama, the company said, declining to name the clients.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
